memory (N*(N+1)) long long = same as full prefix? Actually N*(N+1) ~64M, similar.\n- B full 2D prefix: (N+1)^2 ~64.016M, slightly more.\n\nBoth are fine.\n\nGiven we want to integrate diverse transformations from A,B,C:\n- From A: FastScanner direct buffer cursors.\n- From B: OpenMP parallel for reduction(max) over starting rows, and use long long arithmetic.\n- From C: vertical prefix sums (or full 2D prefix?) Actually C uses vertical prefix sums with sliding window; B uses full 2D prefix. We can choose one.\n\nMaybe combine A's scanner + C's vertical prefix sum approach + B's OpenMP parallelization. That seems a good integration of all three ideas.\n\nLet's implement that. Also add `#pragma omp simd` on the initial window accumulation as in C, and maybe unroll inner loops? We can keep simple.\n\nPotential issue: The input reading loop with fs.nextInt() inside nested loops may be slower than using fread bulk parse; but A's scanner is already fast.\n\nLet's write code:\n\n```cpp\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static constexpr int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    char* cur;\n    char* end;\n\n    bool refill() {\n        size_t r = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n        cur = buf;\n        end = buf + r;\n        return r > 0;\n    }\n\npublic:\n    FastScanner() : cur(buf), end(buf) {}\n\n    inline int nextInt() {\n        while (true) {\n            if (cur == end && !refill()) return 0;\n            char c = *cur++;\n            if (c <= ' ') continue;\n\n            int sign = 1;\n            if (c == '-') {\n                sign = -1;\n                if (cur == end && !refill()) return 0;\n                c = *cur++;\n            }\n\n            int x = c - '0';\n            while (true) {\n                if (cur == end && !refill()) break;\n                char d = *cur++;\n                if (d < '0' || d > '9') break;\n                x = x * 10 + (d - '0');\n            }\n            return sign * x;\n        }\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    const size_t N = (size_t)n;\n    std::vector<long long> pref((N + 1) * N, 0);\n\n    for (size_t i = 1; i <= N; ++i) {\n        const size_t base = i * N;\n        const size_t prev = (i - 1) * N;\n        #pragma omp simd\n        for (size_t j = 0; j < N; ++j) {\n            int v = fs.nextInt();\n            pref[base + j] = pref[prev + j] + v;\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    const size_t limit_i = N - s;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum)\n    for (size_t i = 0; i <= limit_i; ++i) {\n        const long long* top = &pref[i * N];\n        const long long* bottom = &pref[(i + s) * N];\n\n        long long window = 0;\n        #pragma omp simd reduction(+:window)\n        for (size_t j = 0; j < (size_t)s; ++j) {\n            window += bottom[j] - top[j];\n        }\n        long long curMax = window;\n\n        for (size_t j = s; j < N; ++j) {\n            window += (bottom[j] - top[j]) - (bottom[j - s] - top[j - s]);\n            if (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n        }\n\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum, curMax);\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\nBut note: The `#pragma omp simd` inside the input reading loop may not be beneficial because fs.nextInt() is sequential and cannot vectorize; also it might cause issues with OpenMP? Actually we can remove that pragma. Also, using size_t for loops may affect performance but fine.\n\nPotential correctness issue: If s == n? Problem says 0 < S < N, so s<n always. limit_i = n-s >=1.\n\nMemory: pref is (n+1)*n long longs; for n=8000 that's ~512MB. Might be too high if memory limit is e.g., 256MB. But B used similar and passed? The measured times suggest maybe test sizes smaller. However, to be safe we could use int for pref if values are small enough? Let's analyze: Each value v can be 